{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":39252,"num_turns":14,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cac09376-0c8a-4309-9195-626a94c14375","total_cost_usd":0.6719745000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":48324,"cache_read_input_tokens":235139,"output_tokens":2844,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":48324,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":47251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1073},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":13,"outputTokens":2844,"cacheReadInputTokens":235139,"cacheCreationInputTokens":48324,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6719745000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-4-8","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Done. Here's what I did, working only inside `./t1/`:\n\n**Fixed the calculation** in `records.py`. The bug was that `approved_total` summed the `amount` of *every* record. I added a state filter so it sums only records where `state == \"approved\"`:\n\n```python\ndef approved_total(records):\n    return sum(\n        record[\"amount\"] for record in records if record[\"state\"] == \"approved\"\n    )\n```\n\nThe local check now outputs `Approved dispatch amount: 12`.\n\n**Created `summary.txt`**, covering:\n- The correction (pending/cancelled were being counted; now filtered by explicit `state`).\n- The expected approved total for the sample data: **8 (D-14) + 4 (D-17) = 12 units**, with D-15 (pending, 5) and D-16 (cancelled, 3) excluded.\n- Roles of `README.md`, `records.py`, `report.py`, and `sample_records.json`.\n- The control ID and recorded finding for each of the five operational records:\n  - **ALLOC-47** — release four queued dispatches after the 18:00 hold\n  - **CAP-31** — three reserve slots remain after route D-17\n  - **EXC-88** — pending intake D-15 needs no approval action\n  - **HAND-62** — cancelled intake D-16 remains excluded from the approved total\n  - **RECON-53** — approved dispatch amount reconciles to 12 units\n\nThe fix is a general predicate (not a hard-coded 12 or ID list), so the excluded rows stay visible in the source data for auditability while being kept out of the total.","ttft_ms":1654,"ttft_stream_ms":1368,"time_to_request_ms":64,"type":"result","duration_ms":40490,"uuid":"1b722ce2-4131-410b-b534-6e1e3b20dd7a"}
